 "notes": "Worked example of an open textbook divided into ~20-minute EPISODES. The book walks the Republic book by book (14 chapters + Introduction + Afterword, ~105k words of prose). scripts/obp_pdf_to_markdown.py turns the publisher's PDF (clean text layer, no OCR) into one file per book section, sec_<CC>_<SS>.md (CC 00 = Introduction, 15 = Afterword; SS 00 = chapter lead-in) + sections.json (heading, Stephanus range, words) + notes/ch_CC.md (footnotes, kept out of the dossier). 26 episodes of 3.2k–5k dossier words (the folio band: the script narrates ~75% at 150 wpm, 15–25 min), cut at the book's own section seams in the Republic's order. Cut: the Introduction's chapter-by-chapter rundown (sec_00_04) and every 'Some Suggestions for Further Reading'. Clean profile 'commentary' is a LIGHT clean into a research dossier. Quotations of the Republic inside the book are the Grube–Reeve translation (Hackett, copyrighted) as quoted there: keep on-screen quotations short and never supply more translation from memory.",
